  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para>Use the following information to answer questions 1 - 4.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>The graph of \(f(x) = 2x + 6\) is graphed below. Answer the questions about the linear function and its key features.</quote>
    </para>
      <para>
          <media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE WITH AN \(x\)-intercepts OF −3 AND \(y\)-intercepts OF 6.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_09_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the value of \(f(-3)\)?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>0</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What key feature of the linear function is the point \((-3,0)\)?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The \(x\)-intercept, or zero</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the slope of the linear function?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>2</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What part of the linear function is the point \((0, 6)\)?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The \(y\)-intercepts
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <para>Use the following information to answer questions 5 - 8.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>The amount of money Adam saves in dollars is shown in the graph below.</quote>
    </para>
      
        <media alt="GRAPH THAT SHOWS THE TOTAL AMOUNT OF MONEY IN DOLLARS AS A FUNCTION OF NUMBER OF DAYS. THE FUNCTION IS A LINE WITH A POSITIVE SLOPE THAT PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 3) AND (1, 6).">
          <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_09_02.jpg"/>
        </media>
      
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the \(y\)-intercept of the graph?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The point is \((0,3)\).
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What does the \(y\)-intercepts mean in the context of the problem</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary.</para>
          <para>When Adam started saving, he already had 3 dollars on
      day 0.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the slope?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>The slope is 3.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What does the slope mean in the context of the problem</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary.</para>
          <para>Every 1 day, Adam saves 3 dollars.
  </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para>Use the following information to answer questions 9 - 12.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>The graph of \(f(x) = 13x + 2\) is graphed below. Identify the appropriate label for each key feature of the graph.</quote>
    </para>
      <para>
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_09_03.png"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <!--Q3a-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the key feature labeled \(A\) on the graph?
    </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>

          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(A\), (0, 2), is the \(y\)-intercept.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q3b-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the key feature labeled \(B\) on the graph?
    </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>

          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(B\), (-6, 0), is the \(x\)-intercept or zero.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q3c-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the key feature labeled \(C\) on the graph?
    </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>

          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(C\), (0, 0), is the origin.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q3d-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the key feature labeled \(D\) on the graph?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>

          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(D\), \(\frac13\), is the slope.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
